<title>FRANCE: Unions call one-day strike at French post office.</title>
<headline>Unions call one-day strike at French post office.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five unions operating at the French post office, La Poste, said on Monday they have called a one-day strike and a national demonstration in Paris for May 28 to protest against restructuring and &quot;any kind of privatisation&quot;.</p>
<p>The CFDT union said in a statement, &quot;This day is a step in the mobilisation of postal workers which will continue in the months to come as long as La Poste persists in refusing to discuss employment and a reduction in working hours.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
